==Distribution==
The cactus is [[endemism|endemic]] to the [[Chihuahuan Desert]], located  in northeastern [[Mexico]].<ref name=Ande01p334>{{Citation |last=Anderson |first=Edward F. |year=2001 |title=The Cactus Family |location=Pentland, Oregon |publisher=Timber Press |isbn=978-0-88192-498-5 }}, p. 334</ref>

It is native to the Méxican states of [[Coahuila]], [[Durango]], [[Nuevo Leon]], [[San Luis Potosí]], and [[Tamaulipas]], found growing on rocky limestone slopes.<ref>[http://cactiguide.com/cactus/?genus=Ferocactus&species=pilosus CactiGuide: ''Ferocactus pilosus'']</ref><ref name="Art 2013 q952">{{cite web | last=Art | first=Cactus | title=Ferocactus pilosus | website=LLIFLE | date=2013-08-04 | url=http://www.llifle.com/Encyclopedia/CACTI/Family/Cactaceae/13424/Ferocactus_pilosus | access-date=2024-02-10}}{{Creative Commons text attribution notice|cc=bysa3|from this source=yes}}</ref>
